    "title": "Daria Vasyutinsky Shapira - ACL Anthology",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "![ACL Logo](https://aclanthology.org/images/acl-logo.svg) ACL Anthology ⟨1⟩\n  * About⟨2⟩\n    * Announcements⟨3⟩\n    * Communication channels⟨4⟩\n    * Related work⟨5⟩\n    * Copyright⟨6⟩\n    * * * *\n    * Credits⟨7⟩\n    * Volunteer⟨8⟩\n    * Development⟨9⟩\n    * Feedback⟨10⟩\n  * Using⟨2⟩\n    * Citing papers⟨11⟩\n    * Links in the Anthology⟨12⟩\n    * Data access⟨13⟩\n    * * * *\n    * All FAQs⟨14⟩\n    * * * *\n    * ###### Details\n    * Anthology identifiers⟨15⟩\n    * Names⟨16⟩\n    * ORCID iDs⟨17⟩\n    * DOIs⟨18⟩\n    * Verified authors⟨19⟩\n  * Contributions⟨2⟩\n    * Submissions⟨20⟩\n    * Corrections⟨21⟩\n    * Author pages⟨22⟩\n    * Attachments⟨23⟩\n  * GitHub⟨24⟩\n\n\n##  Daria Vasyutinsky Shapira ⟨22⟩\n* * *\n#### 2025\npdf ⟨25⟩bib ⟨26⟩abs⟨27⟩\n**Systematic Textual Availability of Manuscripts⟨28⟩**  \nHadar Miller⟨29⟩ | Samuel Londner⟨30⟩ | Tsvi Kuflik⟨31⟩ | Daria Vasyutinsky Shapira⟨32⟩ | Nachum Dershowitz⟨33⟩ | Moshe Lavee⟨34⟩  \nProceedings of the 5th Conference on Language, Data and Knowledge⟨35⟩\nThe digital era has made millions of manuscript images in Hebrew available to all. However, despite major advancements in handwritten text recognition over the past decade, an efficient pipeline for large scale and accurate conversion of these manuscripts into useful machine-readable form is still sorely lacking.We propose a pipeline that significantly improves recognition models for automatic transcription of Hebrew manuscripts. Transfer learning is used to fine-tune pretrained models. For post-recognition correction, it leverages text reuse, a common phenomenon in medieval manuscripts, and state-of-the-art large language models for medieval Hebrew.The framework successfully handles noisy transcriptions and consistently suggests alternate, better readings. Initial results show that word level accuracy increased by 10% for new readings proposed by text-reuse detection. Moreover, the character level accuracy improved by 18% by fine-tuning models on the first few pages of each manuscript.\nSearch⟨36⟩\n##### Co-authors\n  * Nachum Dershowitz⟨33⟩ 1\n  * Tsvi Kuflik⟨31⟩ 1\n  * Moshe Lavee⟨34⟩ 1\n  * Samuel Londner⟨30⟩ 1\n  * Hadar Miller⟨29⟩ 1\n\n\n##### Venues\n  * LDK⟨37⟩1\n\n\n Fix author⟨38⟩\n![Creative Commons License](https://i.creativecommons.org/l/by/4.0/88x31.png)⟨39⟩ ACL materials are Copyright © 1963–2026 ACL; other materials are copyrighted by their respective copyright holders. Materials prior to 2016 here are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 International License⟨40⟩. Permission is granted to make copies for the purposes of teaching and research. Materials published in or after 2016 are licensed on a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License⟨41⟩.\nThe ACL Anthology is managed and built by the ACL Anthology team⟨7⟩ of volunteers.\n_Site last built on 22 July 2026 at 14:46 UTC withcommit 280e4ed⟨42⟩._\n",
